 # Truth Pays: Kickback-style deposits for Luma
 
+Multi-event continuation: [canonical project brain](../../PROJECT_BRAIN.md). The unified local product
+lives at the workspace root; this directory preserves v7 and its historical deployment. Follow the
+updated [event-bound import workflow](docs/import-provenance.md): both raw import stages require
+`--provenance-review`, and verified/claims CSV sidecars must be retained. Legacy examples below need
+that additional review argument. Historical policy, deployment inputs and Solidity are unchanged.
+
 Guests who want a guaranteed spot send a **refundable deposit in ETH on Ethereum mainnet** (the amount is `deposit` in `config.json`: 0.01 ETH for now, about $23 on 27 Oct 2026). Guests who show up get their deposit back, **plus an equal share of the no-shows' deposits**. Everyone else can still request a free spot, which the hosts approve by hand. A staker who was there but missed at check-in can challenge the attendance list on **Kleros**.
 
 ```
